.TH LPSD 8 "September 2026" "authd" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lpsd \- Peios local principal source daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/sbin/lpsd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lpsd
owns the local principal database, verifies local credentials, and registers
with the Peios authentication authority as a Principal Source Interface
provider.  It cannot mint or install tokens.
.PP
The daemon also serves the local administration protocol used by
.BR lps (1)
on
.IR /run/lpsd/admin.sock .
It reports ready only after its source registration has been acknowledged by
.BR authd (8).
.PP
The service is normally started by peinit from the registry definition shipped
in
.IR /usr/share/regim/lpsd-service.reg .
It takes no command-line options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/state/lpsd
Persistent local-principal state.
.TP
.I /run/lpsd/admin.sock
Local administration socket.
.TP
.I /run/psi.sock
Authentication-authority source socket.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regim/lpsd-authd-registration.reg
Seed which registers lpsd with the authority.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR authd (8),
.BR lps (1),
.BR login (1)
